      "value": "@{5c71ea27a884dd22f1960ec2|full_name}: The difference between your setup and VRChat's is that VRChat adds the AVPro AudioOutput component at runtime. This means that it's always the last component on the GameObject so it runs its audio code last. The AVPro AudioOutput component uses OnAudioFilterRead to inject the audio from the MediaPlayer into the AudioSource which since this happens after the other audio filters have run they cannot affect it. Unity doesn't expose any methods for rearranging the order of components at runtime so we can't just move the AudioOutput to be above the filters.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
